#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# sign

#% text
# `sign(x)` gives -1, 0 or 1 for a real `x` that is negative, zero or positive.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For a complex number `z` other than 0, `sign(z)` is `z/abs(z)`, a number on the unit circle.

#% item
# Exact constants are decided numerically; a symbol stays unevaluated, and `refine` decides it from the assumptions.

#% item
# `sign` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
sign(-3)
#% output
#= -1

#% cell
sign(0)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
sign(2.5)
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
sign(pi - 3)
#% output
#= 1

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A complex number:

#% cell
sign(3 + 4*im)
#% output
#= 3/5 + 4*im/5

#% text
# Each element of a list:

#% cell
sign([-2, 0, 7])
#% output
#= [-1, 0, 1]

#% text
# A symbol with an assumption:

#% cell
assuming(x > 0, refine(sign(x)))
#% output
#= 1

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `x == sign(x)*abs(x)`:

#% cell
sign(-7.5)*abs(-7.5)
#% output
#= -7.5

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `abs`, `unit_step`, `is_positive`, `is_negative`
